[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3273298583","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110369#issuecomment-3273298583","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110369","id":3273298583,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7DGpKX","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-10T04:41:49Z","updated_at":"2025-09-10T04:45:27Z","body":"> From a usability perspective, changing the index via the spinner is not so intuitive. Then I feel it would be helpful to have a function to move the selected point to either the most top or most bottom (this should allow creating a preferred triangle by applying it any three points in cases where symmetrical quadrilateral occur like #66336).\r\n\r\nIt's possible to type into the index field a number higher than the number of points to clamp it to the top, or a negative number to clamp it to 0. Is this not satisfactory?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3273298583/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3273311945","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110369#issuecomment-3273311945","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110369","id":3273311945,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7DGsbJ","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-10T04:51:15Z","updated_at":"2025-09-10T04:52:40Z","body":"@vaner-org That might be sufficient to some extent. However, since there's no way for users to know this within the editor, it should probably be documented somewhere, like in a tooltip or at least in the documentation. Ideally, right-clicking might bring up options including renaming, but if that's too much work, just the documentation for now should suffice (and I think we can send the right-click option as follow up PR later).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3273311945/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3279387870","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110369#issuecomment-3279387870","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110369","id":3279387870,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Dd3ze","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-11T09:13:44Z","updated_at":"2025-09-11T09:13:44Z","body":"(from rocketchat) I'm not happy about changing from returning a cached StringName name; to calling String get_blend_point_name(int p_point) const; which then must perform itos(i) followed by String -> StringName conversion, at every _process\r\n\r\nIf the names could be cached, I might feel better about it. Or maybe, for compatibility, we should always store the number as the name, and if the name is numeric, then it always uses an index and ignores the name.\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3279387870/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3279661571","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110369#issuecomment-3279661571","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110369","id":3279661571,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7De6oD","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-11T10:02:13Z","updated_at":"2025-09-11T10:20:31Z","body":"@lyuma That case `parameters/blendspace2d/ + get_blend_point_name(0)` exists solely for compatibility with niche scenarios where paths depend on dynamically changing points. If you want to cache the path name in cases where it depends on this dynamic path, you would likely need to handle caching on the user side before and after `add_point()` or `remove_point()`. Alternatively, adding a signal like `points_reordered` could be another approach to consider.\r\n\r\nHowever, as I mentioned above, I believe use cases that rely on paths being dynamically changed are niche. So in most normal cases where you're just accessing path `parameters/blendspace2d/0` (`0` is \"name\", not \"index\") shouldn't affect performance. The current BlendSpace dynamically transcribes index into name using itos, so my suggestion in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110369#discussion_r2335739050 for this PR simply always prevents name from being changed automatically. Furthermore, I argue that inconsistent path behavior depend on whether it is number or not should be avoided, as it can cause confusion.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3279661571/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3414997269","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110369#issuecomment-3414997269","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110369","id":3414997269,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LjLkV","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-17T10:59:00Z","updated_at":"2025-11-28T19:50:33Z","body":"Pending further opinions, I do request that this PR not close #66336, because if the important part that indexes play in animation blending isn't exposed and made apparent to the user, a lot of unpredictable things can occur. I know it caused me a great deal of confusion before I understood it.\r\n\r\nWhile blendpoint indexes remain a necessary evil that hold serious influence over animation blending, I don't think they should be swept under the rug.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3414997269/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3589842145","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110369#issuecomment-3589842145","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110369","id":3589842145,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7V-KTh","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-28T16:17:05Z","updated_at":"2025-11-29T13:09:37Z","body":"In working to address the concerns of the animation team:\r\n\r\n- I have removed the restriction on purely numeric names.\r\n- I now convert index names to String names on first launch post this PR using `get_child_nodes`, to retain compatibility with current code paths, that users can then change into descriptors or clear to get the default creation naming scheme (of \"BlendSpace1D\", \"StateMachine 2\" etc.). If there's a better mechanism for upgrading, I'd appreciate some guidance.\r\n\r\nAs for my own concerns about this PR:\r\n- I have removed the name editing box from the toolbar, after improvements to the inline editor's placement. This not only makes this PR more coherent with StateMachine and AnimationTree, but also helps the toolbar be less cluttered.\r\n- To better address [#66336](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/66336), when the index edit box in the toolbar has focus, all of the labels above the points show their indices rather than their names.\r\n- Additionally, rolling the mousewheel over a blend point increments/decrements the index, while similarly revealing the indices of all points, a timed state that reverts back to names after 1.5 seconds. With this, [opening](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109839), moving, renaming and reordering the index of a blend point can all be done on the point itself rather than via the toolbar.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3589842145/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4000388658","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110369#issuecomment-4000388658","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110369","id":4000388658,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ucRYy","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-04T21:24:47Z","updated_at":"2026-03-04T21:26:20Z","body":"A few questions: \r\n- Failing checks against the extension API. The name must be added as a non-optional member, so has to be before index in `add_blend_point()`. How should I proceed?\r\n- Is there an external need for `_get_triangles()` and `_set_triangles()` in BlendSpace2D? Otherwise I can pull those into the `set`, `get()` and `get_property_list()` and remove `_validate_property()` too.\r\n- Where should I document the new functionality of rolling the mousewheel to change index, and double clicking the text to change the name?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4000388658/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4000574999","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110369#issuecomment-4000574999","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110369","id":4000574999,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7uc-4X","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-04T22:01:31Z","updated_at":"2026-03-04T23:09:15Z","body":"> Failing checks against the extension API. The name must be added as a non-optional member, so has to be before index in add_blend_point(). How should I proceed?\r\n\r\nI think there are two approaches.\r\n\r\n1. Make the string optional, disallowing empty name only when it's `#ifdef DISABLE_DEPRECATED`, and fallback to automatic naming with a warning like `In the future, empty names will be deprecated, so explicitly passing a name is recommended.` in `#else` block, also empty name is prevented by editor (means that warning is only shown by user script)\r\n2. Move the string before the index and rename it as new function like `add_blend_point_with_name()` with comment `TODO: In Godot5, it should become add_blend_point()`, and mark the old API as deprecated in xml like `<method name=\"add_blend_point\" deprecated=\"Will be replaced with add_blend_point_with_name in the future.\">`, and make editor to use `add_blend_point_with_name` only. Then no longer needed to add `.compat.inc`","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4000574999/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4003073818","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110369#issuecomment-4003073818","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110369","id":4003073818,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7umg8a","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-05T07:57:31Z","updated_at":"2026-03-05T07:58:11Z","body":"Regarding approach no. 2, isn't it problematic to say that `add_blend_point` will be replaced with `add_blend_point_with_name` in the future, when actually the latter will be taking the `add_blend_point` name when replacement does happen?\r\n\r\nFor approach no. 1, the current `.compat.inc` and refactors remain, correct? With just an additional `#ifdef DISABLE_DEPRECATED` block inside `add_blend_point`? If so, I'm leaning towards preferring it, since the inferred name can also be conveyed to the user with the warning they are given.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4003073818/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4005397472","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110369#issuecomment-4005397472","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110369","id":4005397472,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7uvYPg","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-05T14:19:41Z","updated_at":"2026-03-05T14:19:41Z","body":"No 2 depends on a future ProjectConverter (as was done from Godot 3 to 4). I think 1 is acceptable for now.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4005397472/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4007656802","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110369#issuecomment-4007656802","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110369","id":4007656802,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7u3_1i","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-05T20:42:04Z","updated_at":"2026-03-05T20:42